IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa6-private-and-public.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries), the cross-headings
-- "Private companies" and "Public companies": ss 270 to 273 (lines 3567-3615 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1 of the part agent coa6: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official text
-- and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are generated by srcrefs.py and checked by it.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). A decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to the case.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a definition that says "means" or "are to"; an "if", "where" or "until"
--               condition; a period the text fixes; a flat negative such as "is not required"). Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent; a list not closed; "includes"; an undefined term; a point outside the
--               sources; a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording and the case falls outside the limit). Each such
--               branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. REFUSE is not used.
--
-- SEAMS. A fact another part or the keel answers is an INPUT named for the section that answers it (PLAN.md section 4). This
-- module imports coa-core only: the keel's answers (s 4(1), s 4(2), s 1173(1) "officer") are inputs of type MAYBE BOOLEAN,
-- because a GIVEN named like an imported keel function shadows it silently (measured on 1.6.110), and the seat layer
-- (coa6-seat.l4) is what imports coa-definitions and wires the keel's answers to these inputs.
--
-- MONEY AND PERIODS. The pounds a "level on the standard scale" stands for are not in the Act: they are inputs, and the
-- numbers used in the tests are illustrations, never the legal figures.

§ `Part 12 -- Company secretaries`

§§ `Private companies`

-- ---- s 270: Private company not required to have secretary ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:3570 | (1) A private company is not required to have a secretary.
@ref s 270(1) Private company not required to have secretary (src:3570)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(1) the company is a private company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A private company is not required to have a secretary"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company is not required to have a secretary" speaks of a private company only
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(1) does not say whether the company is a private company

-- "without a secretary" is a defined phrase: a private company that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption in
-- subsection (1), which is to say a private company that has no secretary.
-- src:3571 | (2) References in the Companies Acts to a private company “without a secretary” are to a private company that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption in subsection (1); and references to a private company “with a secretary” shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 270(2) Private company "without a secretary" (src:3571)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(1) the company is a private company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company for the time being has a secretary`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to a private company “without a secretary” are to a private company that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption in subsection (1)"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to a private company that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(1) does not say whether the company is a private company

-- src:3571 | (2) References in the Companies Acts to a private company “without a secretary” are to a private company that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption in subsection (1); and references to a private company “with a secretary” shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 270(2) Private company "with a secretary" (src:3571)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(2) the company is a private company with a secretary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(1) the company is a private company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company for the time being has a secretary`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to a private company “with a secretary” shall be construed accordingly"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to a private company “with a secretary” shall be construed accordingly"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(1) does not say whether the company is a private company

-- (3)(a)(i): in the case of a private company without a secretary, anything authorised or required to be given or sent to, or
-- served on, the company by being sent to its secretary may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself.
-- Name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: a function named for a grant whose gate is "in the case of" (group (i)) is not flipped: outside the
-- gate it answers JUST FALSE; a thing that is not of the kind described is outside the text's wording and stays NOTHING.
-- src:3572 | (3) In the case of a private company without a secretary—
-- src:3573 | (a) anything authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary—
-- src:3574 | (i) may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself, and
@ref s 270(3)(a)(i) Private company without a secretary: things sent to the secretary (src:3572-3574)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `the company for the time being has a secretary`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, group (i), assumed, not ruled): "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own gate, as a "where" is; the other reading is NOTHING (F-grants)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(1) does not say whether the company is a private company

-- src:3572 | (3) In the case of a private company without a secretary—
-- src:3573 | (a) anything authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary—
-- src:3574 | (i) may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself, and
-- src:3575 | (ii) if addressed to the secretary shall be treated as addressed to the company; and
@ref s 270(3)(a)(ii) Private company without a secretary: things addressed to the secretary (src:3572-3575)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is addressed to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `the company for the time being has a secretary`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary` AND `the thing is addressed to the secretary`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if addressed to the secretary shall be treated as addressed to the company"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a private company without a secretary"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(1) does not say whether the company is a private company

-- (3)(b): anything else required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary may be done by or to (i) a director, or
-- (ii) a person authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors.
-- src:3572 | (3) In the case of a private company without a secretary—
-- src:3576 | (b) anything else required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary of the company may be done by or to—
-- src:3577 | (i) a director, or
-- src:3578 | (ii) a person authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors.
@ref s 270(3)(b) Private company without a secretary: anything else done by or to the secretary (src:3572-3578)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is one of those described in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `the company for the time being has a secretary`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT (`the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary`)) OR `the thing is one of those described in paragraph (a)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything else required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary"
        ELSE IF `the person is authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors`
             THEN JUST TRUE -- limb (ii)
             ELSE CONSIDER `s 250 the person occupies the position of director`
                  WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- limb (i)
                  OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be done by or to— (i) a director, or (ii) a person authorised generally or specifically"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, group (i), assumed, not ruled): "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own gate, as a "where" is; the other reading is NOTHING (F-grants)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(1) does not say whether the company is a private company

§§ `Public companies`

-- ---- s 271: Public company required to have secretary --------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3581 | A public company must have a secretary.
@ref s 271 Public company required to have secretary (src:3581)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271 the public company must have a secretary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must have a secretary" speaks of a public company only
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(2) does not say whether the company is a public company

-- Section 272(1) itself calls not having a secretary being "in breach of section 271 (requirement to have secretary)".
-- src:3581 | A public company must have a secretary.
-- src:3583 | (1) If it appears to the Secretary of State that a public company is in breach of section 271 (requirement to have secretary), the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under this section.
@ref s 271 Public company required to have secretary: in breach (src:3581-3583)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 271 the public company is in breach of section 271` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company has a secretary`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A public company must have a secretary" (the duty is met)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must have a secretary" speaks of a public company only
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(2) does not say whether the company is a public company

-- ---- s 272: Direction requiring public company to appoint secretary -----------------------------------------

-- (1): a power of the Secretary of State, so a failed "if" is NOTHING (a grant is not turned into a bar): name-test sweep of 2026-11-12,
-- test 1 (an "If" gate on a function named for a power); a company that is not a public company is outside "a public company" (a scope limit).
-- src:3583 | (1) If it appears to the Secretary of State that a public company is in breach of section 271 (requirement to have secretary), the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under this section.
@ref s 272(1) Direction requiring public company to appoint secretary (src:3583)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 271` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 272` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 271`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State that a public company is in breach of section 271"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a public company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(2) does not say whether the company is a public company

-- (2): what the direction must state and specify. A bare "must" not done answers JUST FALSE (fork F-must in NOTES.md).
-- src:3584 | (2) The direction must state that the company appears to be in breach of that section and specify—
-- src:3585 | (a) what the company must do in order to comply with the direction, and
-- src:3586 | (b) the period within which it must do so.
@ref s 272(2) Content of the direction: statement and specification (src:3584-3586)
GIVEN `the direction states that the company appears to be in breach of section 271` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction specifies what the company must do in order to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction specifies the period within which the company must do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(2) the direction states and specifies what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the direction states that the company appears to be in breach of section 271`
         AND `the direction specifies what the company must do in order to comply`
         AND `the direction specifies the period within which the company must do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The direction must state that the company appears to be in breach of that section and specify— (a) what the company must do in order to comply with the direction, and (b) the period within which it must do so"

-- (2), closing words: the period "must be not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the
-- direction is given". Months are counted with `add months` (it clamps a day that the later month lacks to that month's last
-- day: fork F-months in NOTES.md); the end of the period is allowed on either limit (fork F-limits).
-- src:3587 | That period must be not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the direction is given.
@ref s 272(2) Content of the direction: the length of the period (src:3587)
GIVEN `the date on which the direction is given` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the direction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` MEANS
    IF       `the last day of the period specified in the direction` AT LEAST `add months` `the date on which the direction is given` 1
         AND `the last day of the period specified in the direction` AT MOST `add months` `the date on which the direction is given` 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That period must be not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the direction is given"

-- src:3588 | (3) The direction must also inform the company of the consequences of failing to comply.
@ref s 272(3) Content of the direction: the consequences (src:3588)
GIVEN `the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(3) the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply` MEANS
    IF `the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The direction must also inform the company of the consequences of failing to comply"

-- (4) and (5): the duty to comply by the end of the period. The "where" of (4) and the "if" of (5) are the text's own
-- conditions, so a case outside each answers JUST FALSE. The notice is "under section 276", which this text shows as repealed
-- (lines 3625-3626): the notice is taken as an input and is not tied to s 276 or to s 279G (finding F-276 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3589 | (4) Where the company is in breach of section 271 it must comply with the direction by—
-- src:3590 | (a) making the necessary appointment, and
-- src:3591 | (b) giving notice of it under section 276,
-- src:3592 | before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 272(4) Duty to comply: company in breach (src:3589-3592)
GIVEN `the company is in breach of section 271` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(4) the company must comply with the direction by making the appointment and giving notice of it` MEANS
    IF `the company is in breach of section 271`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company is in breach of section 271 it must comply with the direction by"

-- src:3593 | (5) If the company has already made the necessary appointment, it must comply with the direction by giving notice of it under section 276 before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 272(5) Duty to comply: appointment already made (src:3593)
GIVEN `the company has already made the necessary appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(5) the company must comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment` MEANS
    IF `the company has already made the necessary appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company has already made the necessary appointment, it must comply with the direction by giving notice"

-- One step of (4) or (5), measured against "the end of the period specified in the direction": done on or before the last day is
-- in time; done after it is not (a period the text fixes: JUST FALSE); not yet done is JUST FALSE once the last day has passed
-- and NOTHING while the period is still running.
-- src:3592 | before the end of the period specified in the direction.
-- src:3593 | (5) If the company has already made the necessary appointment, it must comply with the direction by giving notice of it under section 276 before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 272(4) Duty to comply: before the end of the period (src:3592-3593)
GIVEN `the day the step was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the direction` IS A DATE
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the step was done`
    WHEN JUST day THEN
        IF day AT MOST `the last day of the period specified in the direction`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the period specified in the direction"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day of the question` AT MOST `the last day of the period specified in the direction`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the end of the period specified in the direction" (the period has not ended)
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the period specified in the direction" (it has ended and the step was not taken)

-- Three-valued "both": JUST FALSE if either is, JUST TRUE if both are, otherwise NOTHING.
-- src:3590 | (a) making the necessary appointment, and
-- src:3591 | (b) giving notice of it under section 276,
@ref s 272(4) Duty to comply: both steps (src:3590-3591)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(4) both steps` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3589 | (4) Where the company is in breach of section 271 it must comply with the direction by—
-- src:3590 | (a) making the necessary appointment, and
-- src:3591 | (b) giving notice of it under section 276,
-- src:3592 | before the end of the period specified in the direction.
-- src:3593 | (5) If the company has already made the necessary appointment, it must comply with the direction by giving notice of it under section 276 before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 272(4)-(5) Has the company complied with the direction (src:3589-3593)
GIVEN `the company is in breach of section 271` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has already made the necessary appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the necessary appointment was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day notice of the appointment was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the direction` IS A DATE
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the company is in breach of section 271` AND (NOT (`the company has already made the necessary appointment`))
    THEN `s 272(4) both steps`
             (`s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` `the day the necessary appointment was made` `the last day of the period specified in the direction` `the day of the question`)
             (`s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` `the day notice of the appointment was given` `the last day of the period specified in the direction` `the day of the question`)
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the company is in breach of section 271`)) AND `the company has already made the necessary appointment`
         THEN `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` `the day notice of the appointment was given` `the last day of the period specified in the direction` `the day of the question`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither "Where the company is in breach of section 271" nor "If the company has already made the necessary appointment" holds (or both are said to hold)

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The clock is days counted from the day the direction is given (time 0); the last day of the
-- period is `days until the last day`. (4) needs both steps, in either order (RAND); (5) needs the notice. Run with #TRACE in
-- the tests file: a DEONTIC cannot be compared in an #ASSERT, so the decision function above is what the assertions count.
-- src:3589 | (4) Where the company is in breach of section 271 it must comply with the direction by—
-- src:3590 | (a) making the necessary appointment, and
-- src:3591 | (b) giving notice of it under section 276,
-- src:3592 | before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 272(4) Duty to comply (regulative) (src:3589-3592)
GIVEN `days until the last day of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 272(4) the company's duty as a regulative rule` MEANS
        (   PARTY Company
            MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "make the necessary appointment (s 272(4)(a))"
            WITHIN `days until the last day of the period`
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the appointment was not made before the end of the period specified in the direction (s 272(4))")
    RAND
        (   PARTY Company
            MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the appointment (s 272(4)(b))"
            WITHIN `days until the last day of the period`
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BECAUSE "notice was not given before the end of the period specified in the direction (s 272(4))")

-- src:3593 | (5) If the company has already made the necessary appointment, it must comply with the direction by giving notice of it under section 276 before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 272(5) Duty to comply (regulative) (src:3593)
GIVEN `days until the last day of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 272(5) the company's duty as a regulative rule` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the appointment (s 272(5))"
    WITHIN `days until the last day of the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "notice was not given before the end of the period specified in the direction (s 272(5))"

-- (6): the offence. The company commits it "if" it fails to comply with the direction: a failed "if" answers JUST FALSE
-- (marginal reading (a)); the answer of s 272(4)-(5) is taken as the input.
-- src:3594 | (6) If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:3595 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 272(6)(a) Offence: the company (src:3594-3595)
GIVEN `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(6)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by (a) the company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company fails to comply" (whether it has failed is not yet settled)

-- (6), closing words: "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company."
-- src:3597 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 272(6) Offence: a shadow director is treated as an officer (src:3597)
GIVEN `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(6) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a shadow director is treated as an officer" says nothing of a person who is not one
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 251 does not say whether the person is a shadow director

-- (6)(b): "every officer of the company who is in default". The person is an officer if the keel's s 1173(1) says so (it answers
-- NOTHING for "another position": "includes") or is a shadow director (the deeming above).
-- src:3594 | (6) If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:3596 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:3597 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 272(6)(b) Offence: every officer in default (src:3594-3597)
GIVEN `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company fails to comply" (whether it has failed is not yet settled)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF       (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             OR (`s 272(6) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` `s 251 the person is a shadow director` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 does not say whether the officer is in default
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by (a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default" names no one else

-- (7): "liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a
-- daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale" followed, with nothing between them but a full
-- stop's absence, by "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale". The rendering has run two wordings
-- together (it may carry more than one extent version of a provision, meta.json text_caveat) and does not say where each
-- applies: fork F-272-7 in NOTES.md. The caller says which wording is meant; NOTHING means unknown.
-- src:3598 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 272(7) Penalty: the two wordings (src:3598)
DECLARE `s 272(7) wording of the daily default fine` IS ONE OF
    `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`
    `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`

-- core's `Fine limit` has no constructor for "one-tenth of the greater of an amount in pounds and a level" (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:3598 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 272(7) Penalty: the daily default fine limit (src:3598)
DECLARE `s 272(7) daily default fine limit` IS ONE OF
    `s 272(7) a fraction of a level on the standard scale` HAS `s 272(7) fraction of the level` IS A NUMBER, `s 272(7) the level` IS A NUMBER
    `s 272(7) a fraction of the greater of an amount in pounds and a level on the standard scale` HAS `s 272(7) fraction of the greater amount` IS A NUMBER, `s 272(7) the amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER, `s 272(7) the other level` IS A NUMBER

-- src:3598 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 272(7) Penalty: the penalty (src:3598)
DECLARE `s 272(7) penalty` HAS
    `s 272(7) how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
    `s 272(7) fine not exceeding` IS A `Fine limit`
    `s 272(7) daily default fine for continued contravention` IS A `s 272(7) daily default fine limit`

-- src:3598 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 272(7) Penalty (src:3598)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      wording IS A MAYBE `s 272(7) wording of the daily default fine`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 272(7) penalty`
`s 272(7) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 272` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable on summary conviction"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER wording
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rendering does not say which of its two wordings of the daily default fine applies
        WHEN JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` THEN
            JUST (`s 272(7) penalty` OF `how the person is convicted`
                      , `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1
                      , `s 272(7) a fraction of a level on the standard scale` 0.1 5)
        WHEN JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale` THEN
            JUST (`s 272(7) penalty` OF `how the person is convicted`
                      , `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1
                      , `s 272(7) a fraction of the greater of an amount in pounds and a level on the standard scale` 0.1 5000 4)

-- In pounds. The pounds that level 5 and level 4 stand for are not in the Act: inputs.
-- src:3598 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 272(7) Penalty: the fine in pounds (src:3598)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272(7) the most a person guilty of an offence may be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`

-- src:3598 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 272(7) Penalty: the daily default fine in pounds (src:3598)
GIVEN wording IS A MAYBE `s 272(7) wording of the daily default fine`
      `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER wording
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rendering does not say which of its two wordings of the daily default fine applies
    WHEN JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` THEN JUST (`the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` DIVIDED BY 10)
    WHEN JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale` THEN
        JUST ((IF `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for` AT LEAST 5000 THEN `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for` ELSE 5000) DIVIDED BY 10)

-- ---- s 273: Qualifications of secretaries of public companies ------------------------------------------------

-- (3): the bodies. "The bodies referred to in subsection (2)(b) are—" is read as a closed list (fork F-273-lists).
-- src:3608 | (3) The bodies referred to in subsection (2)(b) are—
-- src:3609 | (a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales;
-- src:3610 | (b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland;
-- src:3611 | (c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants;
-- src:3612 | (d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland;
-- src:3613 | (e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators;
-- src:3614 | (f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants;
-- src:3615 | (g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy.
@ref s 273(3) The bodies specified in subsection (3) (src:3608-3615)
DECLARE `s 273(3) body` IS ONE OF
    `s 273(3)(a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales`
    `s 273(3)(b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland`
    `s 273(3)(c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants`
    `s 273(3)(d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland`
    `s 273(3)(e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators`
    `s 273(3)(f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants`
    `s 273(3)(g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy`
    `s 273(3) any other body`

-- src:3608 | (3) The bodies referred to in subsection (2)(b) are—
-- src:3609 | (a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales;
-- src:3610 | (b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland;
-- src:3611 | (c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants;
-- src:3612 | (d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland;
-- src:3613 | (e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators;
-- src:3614 | (f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants;
-- src:3615 | (g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy.
@ref s 273(3) The bodies specified (src:3608-3615)
GIVEN body IS A `s 273(3) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `s 273(3) any other body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The bodies referred to in subsection (2)(b) are—" (a list of seven)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2)(a): "for at least three of the five years immediately preceding his appointment as secretary". The person states how many
-- of those five years, added together, they held the office (fork F-273-2a).
-- src:3604 | (a) that he has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding his appointment as secretary;
@ref s 273(2)(a) Qualification: three of the five years (src:3604)
GIVEN `years in the five years immediately preceding the appointment that the person held the office of secretary of a public company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(2)(a) the person has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding the appointment` MEANS
    IF `years in the five years immediately preceding the appointment that the person held the office of secretary of a public company` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The qualifications are— (a) that he has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding his appointment as secretary"

-- src:3605 | (b) that he is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3);
-- src:3608 | (3) The bodies referred to in subsection (2)(b) are—
-- src:3609 | (a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales;
-- src:3610 | (b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland;
-- src:3611 | (c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants;
-- src:3612 | (d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland;
-- src:3613 | (e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators;
-- src:3614 | (f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants;
-- src:3615 | (g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy.
@ref s 273(2)(b) Qualification: member of a specified body (src:3605-3615)
GIVEN `the bodies of which the person is a member` IS A LIST OF `s 273(3) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(2)(b) the person is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN b YIELD `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` b EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the bodies of which the person is a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The qualifications are— (b) that he is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)"

-- src:3606 | (c) that he is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom;
@ref s 273(2)(c) Qualification: barrister, advocate or solicitor (src:3606)
DECLARE `s 273(2)(c) calling` IS ONE OF
    `s 273(2)(c) a barrister`
    `s 273(2)(c) an advocate`
    `s 273(2)(c) a solicitor`
    `s 273(2)(c) another calling`

-- src:3606 | (c) that he is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom;
@ref s 273(2)(c) Qualification: barrister, advocate or solicitor (src:3606)
GIVEN calling IS A `s 273(2)(c) calling`
      `the person is called or admitted in a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` MEANS
    IF `the person is called or admitted in a part of the United Kingdom`
    THEN CONSIDER calling
         WHEN `s 273(2)(c) another calling` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that he is a barrister, advocate or solicitor"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom"

-- src:3607 | (d) that he is a person who, by virtue of his holding or having held any other position or his being a member of any other body, appears to the directors to be capable of discharging the functions of secretary of the company.
@ref s 273(2)(d) Qualification: capable in the directors' view (src:3607)
GIVEN `it appears to the directors that, by virtue of the person's holding or having held any other position or being a member of any other body, the person is capable of discharging the functions of secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(2)(d) the person is a person who appears to the directors to be capable of discharging the functions of secretary` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the directors that, by virtue of the person's holding or having held any other position or being a member of any other body, the person is capable of discharging the functions of secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The qualifications are— (d) that he is a person who, by virtue of his holding or having held any other position or his being a member of any other body, appears to the directors to be capable"

-- (2): the person has one or more of the qualifications. A limb that answers NOTHING leaves the answer NOTHING unless another
-- limb is JUST TRUE.
-- src:3603 | (2) The qualifications are—
-- src:3604 | (a) that he has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding his appointment as secretary;
-- src:3605 | (b) that he is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3);
-- src:3606 | (c) that he is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom;
-- src:3607 | (d) that he is a person who, by virtue of his holding or having held any other position or his being a member of any other body, appears to the directors to be capable of discharging the functions of secretary of the company.
@ref s 273(2) The qualifications (src:3603-3607)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      d IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` MEANS
    IF (a EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (b EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (c EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (d EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (a EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (b EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (c EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (d EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The qualifications are— (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ..." and none holds
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not settled

-- (1)(a): "is a person who appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of
-- secretary of the company" (the directors' view, so an input).
-- src:3601 | (a) is a person who appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company, and
@ref s 273(1)(a) The directors' view of the secretary (src:3601)
GIVEN `it appears to the directors that the person has the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(a) the secretary is a person who appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the directors that the person has the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a person who appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company"

-- (1), for one secretary: both (a) and (b), where (b) is "has one or more of the following qualifications".
-- src:3600 | (1) It is the duty of the directors of a public company to take all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary (or each joint secretary) of the company—
-- src:3601 | (a) is a person who appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company, and
-- src:3602 | (b) has one or more of the following qualifications.
@ref s 273(1) What the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure (src:3600-3602)
GIVEN `s 273(1)(a) the secretary is a person who appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1) the secretary has what the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure` MEANS
    IF (`s 273(1)(a) the secretary is a person who appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to secure that the secretary ... (a) is a person who appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience ..., and (b) has one or more of the following qualifications"
    ELSE IF (`s 273(1)(a) the secretary is a person who appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not settled

-- (1), "the secretary (or each joint secretary)": every one of them. No secretary at all is not covered (silent).
-- src:3600 | (1) It is the duty of the directors of a public company to take all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary (or each joint secretary) of the company—
@ref s 273(1) The secretary or each joint secretary (src:3600)
GIVEN `the answers for the secretary or for each joint secretary` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1) the secretary or each joint secretary has what the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure` MEANS
    IF `the answers for the secretary or for each joint secretary` EQUALS EMPTY
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no secretary or joint secretary to ask about
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN x YIELD x EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers for the secretary or for each joint secretary`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the secretary (or each joint secretary) of the company"
         ELSE IF all (GIVEN x YIELD x EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers for the secretary or for each joint secretary`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not settled

-- (1): the duty of the directors of a public company. The duty is to take "all reasonable steps": whether they have is the
-- directors' own conduct, taken as an input.
-- src:3600 | (1) It is the duty of the directors of a public company to take all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary (or each joint secretary) of the company—
@ref s 273(1) The duty of the directors of a public company (src:3600)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1) the directors are under a duty to take all reasonable steps` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is the duty of the directors of a public company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 4(2) does not say whether the company is a public company

-- src:3600 | (1) It is the duty of the directors of a public company to take all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary (or each joint secretary) of the company—
@ref s 273(1) Duty performed (src:3600)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors have taken all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary has what subsection (1) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1) the directors have performed their duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 273(1) the directors are under a duty to take all reasonable steps` `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the directors have taken all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary has what subsection (1) describes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is the duty of the directors of a public company to take all reasonable steps" (a bare duty not performed)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the directors of a public company"
